      "marks": 3,
      "answer": "$\\frac{dy}{dx}=-2\\sin\\theta\\cos^3\\theta$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "State $dx/d\\theta=\\sec^2\\theta$ or $dy/d\\theta=-2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta$ — B1, CWO, AEF.\n\nUse $dy/dx=(dy/d\\theta)\\div(dx/d\\theta)$ — M1.\n\nObtain $dy/dx=-2\\sin\\theta\\cos^3\\theta$ from correct working — A1, AG.\n\nAlternative method: convert to Cartesian form and differentiate — M1, with $y=1/(1+x^2)$; obtain $dy/dx=-2x/(1+x^2)^2$ — A1, OE; obtain $dy/dx=-2\\sin\\theta\\cos^3\\theta$ from correct working — A1, AG.\n\nTotal [3].",
